<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Zhex is an experimental Forth-inspired language for readable composition. Explore working examples and try the Go interpreter.">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#153c32">
  <title>Zhex — A Forth-inspired language</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header wrap">
    <a class="wordmark" href="./" aria-label="Zhex home"><img src="favicon.svg" width="34" height="34" alt="">Zhex</a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="examples.html">Examples</a>
      <a href="#start">Get started</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/desireco/zhex">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A Forth-inspired language</p>
        <h1 id="intro-title">Small words.<br>Clear programs.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Small functions fit together through explicit flows. Named values and checked types keep the code easy to follow.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="examples.html">Read the examples <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="#start">Try Zhex locally <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="status"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Experimental · Working Go interpreter</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-example">
        <div class="code-label"><span>hello.zhex</span><span>Console input → output</span></div>
        <pre><code>{{.HeroSource}}</code></pre>
        <div class="terminal-preview"><span class="terminal-label">With input <strong>{{.HeroInput}}</strong></span><samp>{{.HeroOutput}}</samp></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="purpose section" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
      <div class="wrap purpose-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">The direction</p><h2 id="purpose-title">A language for<br>useful work.</h2></div>
        <div class="purpose-copy"><p>We want programs that are easy to reason about and efficient to run.</p><p>The goal is a modular language for command-line tools, games, web applications, and database software.</p><p class="aside">Today, the interpreter runs small programs. Modules and native compilation are planned.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="examples-section section wrap" aria-labelledby="examples-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start with code</p><h2 id="examples-title">See how it reads.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="examples.html">View examples <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="example-links">
        <a href="examples.html#hello"><span class="example-number">01</span><span><strong>Hello, console.</strong><span>Read a name and print a greeting.</span></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="examples.html#fizzbuzz"><span class="example-number">02</span><span><strong>FizzBuzz</strong><span>Combine conditions, loops, and output.</span></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="examples.html#fibonacci"><span class="example-number">03</span><span><strong>Fibonacci</strong><span>Calculate a result with local state.</span></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="examples.html#palindrome"><span class="example-number">04</span><span><strong>Palindrome</strong><span>Read text and check its reverse.</span></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="start-section section wrap" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Run it yourself</p>
      <h2 id="start-title">Run your first<br>Zhex program.</h2>
      <p>Build and run with Go 1.23 or newer.</p>
      <pre class="commands"><code>git clone https://github.com/desireco/zhex.git
cd zhex
go run ./cmd/zhex run examples/hello.zhex</code></pre>
      <p class="access-note">The source repository is currently private. These commands require repository access.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer wrap"><a class="wordmark" href="./">Zhex</a><p>An experimental Forth-inspired language.</p><a href="https://github.com/desireco/zhex/blob/main/docs/initial-language.md">Language reference <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></footer>
</body>
</html>
